From e488969ef413400d3918e230cff236843c33c4ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: schoeremy <jeremyfroeb2007@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 13:13:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 50/65] nxshader, nxhost: run geometry shaders as Metal mesh
 shaders

Metal has no geometry stage; draws whose program has one were dropped (the
geometry shader was even taken for the vertex shader). Splatoon 3 has 83
geometry shaders, all triangle-strip emitters with 3 to 15 vertices.

nxshader::translate_geometry builds one library per vertex + geometry pair:
the vertex shader becomes a plain function, and the mesh entry runs it for
the vertices of its input primitive (primitive assembly for points, lines,
line strips, triangles, strips and fans, indexed or not), then the geometry
code: ALD with a vertex register reads that vertex's outputs, AST writes the
current output vertex, OUT.EMIT appends it to the mesh and closes strip
triangles with the right winding, OUT.CUT restarts the strip,
SR_INVOCATION_INFO reports the input vertex count. VMAD and VSETP now select
bytes/halves like the hardware (the geometry prologue computes vertex
indices with them). All 83 shaders translate and compile (shgeo tool).

The host keeps the geometry stage's buffers and textures (NVN stage 2),
builds a mesh pipeline and draws one single-thread threadgroup per primitive
and instance.

Diagnostics: NX_TRACE_3D_TARGETS, NX_TRACE_3D_TEXTURES, readback values in
NX_TRACE_CPU_TARGETS.

